            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe the case of a man with severe left coronary ostial stenosis who was treated with direct left main angioplasty with a pericardial patch. This approach may be superior to artery bypass grafting in certain patients.</AbstractText>
